# Frontend rules

## Structure
- React function components in JSX (no TypeScript).
- One folder per component with `Name.jsx` and `Name.css`. Pages in `resources/js/pages`, layouts in `resources/js/layouts`, helpers in `resources/js/lib`.
- Reuse the shared components (Button, Modal, FormField, Card). Do not duplicate them.

## Styling
- Plain CSS only. No Tailwind and no CSS-in-JS.
- Global design tokens are CSS variables in one global file: `:root` for the light theme and a dark theme override. Dark is the default and the choice is persisted.
- `html { font-size: 62.5% }` (1rem = 10px). Use rem for sizes.
- Follow the "Identidade visual" section of `docs/product-vision.md` (colors, font Plus Jakarta Sans, radius 0.75rem, purple gradient on primary buttons, cursor glow).
- Income and positive values in purple, expenses and negative values in red, always with a + or - sign.

## Behavior
- The frontend only displays what the API returns. Never compute balances or totals in the browser.
- Create and edit happen in modals.
- Currency with `Intl.NumberFormat('pt-BR', { style: 'currency', currency: 'BRL' })`. Dates as dd/mm/yyyy.
- All UI text in Brazilian Portuguese. Every page has a title and a subtitle.
- Basic accessibility: labels on inputs, visible focus, never rely only on color.
- Show a short empty state with a shortcut when a block depends on data the user has not created yet.
- Desktop only: do not build mobile layouts.